.TH TTYNAME 3
.SH NAME
ttyname, isatty, ttyslot \- find name of a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "char *ttyname(fildes)"
.sp
.B "isatty(fildes)"
.sp
.B "ttyslot()"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ttyname
returns a pointer to the null-terminated path name of the terminal
device associated with file descriptor
.IR fildes .
.PP
.B isatty
returns 1 if
.I fildes
is associated with a terminal device, 0 otherwise.
.PP
.B ttyslot
returns the number of the entry in the
.BR ttys (4)
file for the control
terminal of the current process.
.PP
Note that for every process
.B /dev/tty
is synonymous with the process'
control terminal.
.SH FILES
.nf
/dev/*
/etc/ttys
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
ioctl(2), ttys(4)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B ttyname
returns a null pointer (0) if
.I fildes
does not describe a terminal
device in directory `/dev'.
.PP
.B ttyslot
returns 0 if `/etc/ttys' is inaccessible or if it cannot determine the
control terminal.
.SH BUGS
The return value points to static data whose content is overwritten by
each call.
.sp
